Z||000000||fotofrank||09-16-1999||02:04 PM||||Gents,and Gals: I have an '84 2.5l. Will replaceing the stock TBI with the Holley TBI improve performance? If so how much(very notice able,noticable,hardly noticable)?<BR>I am also planing to have my engin rebuildt because I have some blow-by. Is the kit from the Fiero Store a good bet?||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||09-16-1999||04:11 PM||||wait until after the rebuilt and a port/polish job before changing the TBI unit. That way you can work out the rebuild bugs and know where you are starting.<P>The bigger TBI from holley should help. how much depends on a few things. If your existing TBI unit is in sad shape, then replacing it with the holley should be only slightly more money than a stock one. The holley unit is only diferant from the stock 300 unit in the main bore & buterfly. Otherwise it's just another 300 to the system. Should boost it a bit.<P>consider replacing the cam with the roller type cam/lifter setup from a 86 plus if posible. This reduces cam load by a huge amount. Makes timing gears last much longer.||||reg||2
